WEBVTT

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:35.100
Jyuusan-hime, who had entered the Imperial Residence as a candidate to be Ryuuki's wife,

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.950
looked almost identical to Shuurei.

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:42.530
Shuurei was ordered to become Jyuusan-hime's double,

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:47.330
but the assassins were aiming to kill both Jyuusan-hime and Shuurei.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.550
I... want to be a horse.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.120
I'll be angry at you if you say "Congratulations."

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:14.480
I won't.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:21.570
Do you feel a bit j-jealous?

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.750
I wonder. Perhaps a bit.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.580
I was taken aback when I heard Jyuusan-hime was coming.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:28.940
Really?!

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:30.000
Yes.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.580
Well, I'd be jealous if Seiran took a wife too.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:37.440
However, when you're betrothed to your future wife,

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.090
I'll do my best to be happy from the bottom of my heart.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:47.430
By the way, Ryuuki, I heard that Ran-shogun is taking a break,

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.100
but what happened to Kouyuu-sama?

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.500
A strange rumor is circulating,

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.860
but Kouyuu is just extremely busy, that's all.

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:57.000
If you're feeling lonely, why don't you go and see him?

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.640
He'll scold me if I disturb him.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:02.120
Then apologize and leave.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:06.630
You never consider that when you come to see me, do you?

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:08.800
Yeah, that's true.

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:14.410
Ran-shogun said that he likes you.

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:15.550
I know.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:19.600
Come to think of it, is Tousen Court...

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:23.460
Is this place really all right like that?

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.180
Like what?

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.280
The security's full of holes.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:29.100
What?

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:32.880
It can't be...

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:35.110
Could it?

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.370
What?!

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:57.600
I was told that if you scold me for
disturbing you, I only have to leave.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.970
By Shuurei?

00:03:58.970 --> 00:03:59.720
Yes.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:06.010
She's become a good adviser.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:07.900
Come in.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:12.320
I can spare some time to drink that with you.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:15.650
I was getting fed up with work anyway.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:32.540
The attempt will take place on the night of the new moon.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:35.210
Something's going to happen soon.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:37.910
You've got that worried look again.

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:41.180
Tan-tan!

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:50.060
I was wondering why this mission was given to both me and Seiga.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.960
Because they couldn't rely on you alone?

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:57.620
Then all the more reason to leave it all to Seiga.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:58.460
True.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:03.280
What if Seiga has too many other tasks?

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.900
But that's the norm.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.300
You're incredible, Tan-tan. You're probably right.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:12.020
Seiga is working on some other business.

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:13.950
Precisely.

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:23.340
I thought I should give this to you
the next time we met, Anjuu-sama.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:24.270
A peach?

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:30.100
It's my favorite fruit, but why the odd
combination of one whole and one piece?

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:35.410
Kouki-sama said that if I received a peach from you,
my life would be filled with misfortune,

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:37.850
so I thought I'd return the exact amount back.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:44.590
He's so rude, calling my goodwill gesture a "peach of misfortune."

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:47.860
Huh? Did he say misfortune?

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.870
When you said "Precisely," you meant Seiga, right?

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.830
Did I say that?

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.120
What will you give me today?

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:02.130
I'll drop my princess disguise immediately,

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:05.970
put on a fake moustache and goatee, and dress up as a filthy soldier.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:08.660
Don't, that would be a waste.

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:12.320
Fine, if you'll peel this peach for me,

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:15.490
I'll chat with you while I eat it.

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:17.640
Well, I could do that.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:22.150
Thank you for surrendering to such a simple threat.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:38.910
W-Well... umm...

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:44.920
All that Seiga's done is drag me around as a decoy.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:47.920
Because he wants information on the assassins?

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:51.930
In that case, he's definitely looking for a lead on the assassination plan:

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:56.180
the assassination of someone even
more important than Jyuusan-hime.

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:59.540
Anjuu-sama,

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:06.310
do you know of any high-ranking provincial officials who have died suddenly in the last few months?

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:08.690
Rather, how many do you know of?

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:18.410
I know of...

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:20.290
five.

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:21.760
Five...

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:24.340
Thank you.

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:25.770
Tan-tan, come with me.

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:26.340
What?

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:27.460
Hey!

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:32.220
Will Kouki scold me?

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:34.060
Whatever.

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:38.830
That's right.

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:41.680
Could you please find out if there's some common factor

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:43.730
among those provincial officials who have died recently?

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:45.360
What about you?

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:46.610
I'm going to the Ministry of Civil Service.

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:48.480
What happened before their deaths is important...

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:52.860
but what happened afterwards might be even more important.

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:54.040
See you!

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:01.540
The security's full of holes.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:06.240
Jyuusan-hime and I, indeed the entire Imperial Residence, were the decoys.

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:07.940
Their real target is elsewhere.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:11.580
That's right. Seiga sets his traps slowly.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:16.090
I can still make it. Two more days until the new moon.

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:20.230
Two more days...

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:25.320
The security is perfect, perhaps too perfect.

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:30.120
If he gives himself away...

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:33.250
this will be the easiest job I've ever done.

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:37.480
It all fits.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:40.000
It's just as I thought.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:41.350
Thanks, Tan-tan!

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:46.040
Umm, I don't get it at all.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:47.810
Now then, let's go!

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:49.520
What? Again?!

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:04.980
What?

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:10.520
You over there, weren't you the Governor of Sashuu?

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:13.150
That's right!

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:14.300
Ensei!

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.030
What on earth are you doing in here?

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:19.230
W-Well, it's a long story.

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:22.880
Well, I rescued a woman who was being attacked by hooligans.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:25.780
I got into a fight with them, and then...

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:27.510
Don't slur the end of your sentences!

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:32.050
And then the officers caught you and threw you in here?

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:46.180
Have you been eating and sleeping properly? Are you well?

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.190
Yes.

00:09:55.770 --> 00:09:57.470
Why are you in Kiyou?

00:09:57.470 --> 00:09:59.320
The national exam doesn't start anytime soon, right?

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:03.100
That old man, Kai Yu, said I should go early and prepare for it.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:06.080
Well, that isn't the only reason, though.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:09.790
Is he your assistant, Princess?

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:13.160
You two really are deeply in love with each other.

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:15.460
Sure we are.

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:20.090
So, Princess, is there anything I can do?

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:25.790
Well then, Ensei, I'm counting on you.

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:26.660
Okay.

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:30.890
Where to now?

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:32.990
Tan-tan, you should go back now.

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:38.060
I'm going to make a quick visit to Seiran, and then find Jyuusan-hime.

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:44.680
Jyuusan-hime.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.510
I know.

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:49.070
You want to talk it over face-to-face, right?

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:51.070
That's right.

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:53.500
Please, come over here and sit in front of me.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:55.120
Can't I run away?

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:58.390
No, never. Even if you say it cutely, still no.

00:10:58.390 --> 00:11:00.510
Damn, I guess I can't escape from this.

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:08.050
I-Isn't this a bit too close?

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:09.720
It's a "face-to-face" talk, right?

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:11.970
Besides, we can't be overheard as easily if we're close.

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:12.770
So...

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:17.280
I suppose this is about the one-eyed, dark-skinned man?

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:19.780
Yes.

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:24.370
Umm, before that, I'll tell you why I came here.

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:29.160
My older triplet brothers are always planning how best to proceed.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:33.510
I believe they sent me to the Imperial Residence now for a reason.

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:38.050
They probably want to see what kind of decisions the Emperor will make, and how he'll react,

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:40.890
while providing him with just one way out.

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:44.300
You mean they're judging Ryuuki's capabilities?

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:49.180
If the Emperor doesn't find that one way out,
then that's the end of the game.

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:52.120
But if he does...

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:58.300
They've put in a lot of effort to push the Emperor as far as they can.

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:02.020
That means the reward for the game must be worthwhile.

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:04.460
So is Ran-shogun also included in the reward?

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:07.070
I wouldn't know.

00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:10.790
Anyway, if you know Shuuei-nii-sama's character,

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:15.540
you know he'd never accept the iris again after returning it.

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:16.870
Yes.

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:19.090
No matter what happens, he won't...

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:22.300
even if the Emperor gets down on his knees and begs.

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:28.860
Well, we've digressed a bit, but I put off talking about the mystery man

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:32.710
because I thought that would lead us to the best outcome.

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:33.830
The best outcome?

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:41.210
I think I was chosen this time because of the one-eyed man.

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:44.790
He's the cog that pulls Shuuei-nii-sama and me into this plot.

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:47.570
Is he someone that Ran-shogun knows well?

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:51.070
Please let me handle this for a little while.

00:12:51.070 --> 00:12:53.830
I know I haven't given a sufficient reason.

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:00.590
Will you tell me everything when this is all over?

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:02.620
I promise.

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:07.340
Very well. On the night of the new moon, I'll leave the Imperial Residence to you.

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:14.450
One last thing: did you happen to run into some incompetent assassins during your journey?

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:15.300
I did.

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:20.900
Great! Did you see any marks on their foreheads?

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:22.400
Marks?

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:23.800
Of condemned men.

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:32.660
Not on all of them, but yes.

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:12.170
Fools!

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:26.260
I can't believe he's given the command.

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:32.430
I thought so.

00:14:37.700 --> 00:14:40.510
He'll come, for sure.

00:14:52.610 --> 00:14:54.870
Are you hurt, Yuushun-dono?

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:57.870
I'm fine. Thank you, Seiran-dono.

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:05.840
The Emperor has ordered me to act as your personal bodyguard.

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:09.380
Even if you chase me away because you think that you don't need me, I'll protect you.

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:11.340
You've changed for the better.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:13.810
Before, you'd have gone to Shuurei-dono immediately.

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:21.390
Oujo-sama was the one who warned me about tonight.

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:25.770
Shuurei-dono even took me into consideration?

00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:30.680
I assumed that Inspector Riku had left me out on purpose,

00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:34.150
to test whether Shuurei-dono would notice my situation.

00:15:34.150 --> 00:15:36.700
He's laughing at all of us.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:40.780
Who does he think he is? He's so full of himself.

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:45.460
But he's an outstanding official. He'll go far.

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:49.670
Rest assured, when he does, oujo-sama will as well.

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:55.590
Oh, by the way, a big eater's supposed to arrive from Sashuu soon.

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:59.810
In fact, he should've arrived by now.

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:35.710
Please stand back!

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:42.520
You've come to take the life of the Vice Minister of Arms?

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:45.520
Indeed.

00:16:45.760 --> 00:16:48.760
You've placed your soldiers well, following military strategy.

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:51.530
You have the makings of a tactician.

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:55.960
If a mere assassin can get by my soldiers, then I still have a lot to learn.

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:57.940
Then study harder.

00:16:57.940 --> 00:16:59.180
Now...

00:17:11.650 --> 00:17:12.980
Be careful!

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:14.010
There's another assassin!

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:15.800
That assassin's going to attack from the back!

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:42.340
Aim for the one-eyed man!

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:48.540
The other one's here just to confuse us.

00:17:57.740 --> 00:18:01.140
I can't let you kill the Vice Minister yet.

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:02.450
"Yet"?

00:18:03.110 --> 00:18:05.520
I see, you...

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:28.750
Seiga, are you dead?!

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:30.600
You've got some nerve.

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:32.910
Oh, I'm sorry. It just slipped out.

00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:34.570
Is this a time for jokes?

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:35.520
Of course.

00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:36.250
Ensei!

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:37.760
Yeah, yeah.

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:49.920
He's very... strong.

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:13.740
If I had time, I'd fight you to my heart's content,

00:19:13.740 --> 00:19:16.970
but time's up. I still need to go somewhere.

00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:20.970
In any case, I've accomplished half of my mission.

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:29.690
H-Halt!

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:36.250
Damn...

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:41.670
How did you know we'd be here?

00:19:41.670 --> 00:19:46.740
The Vice Minister of Arms gave the order to hide Jyuusan-hime in Tousen Court, right?

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:47.450
Yeah.

00:19:47.770 --> 00:19:50.960
Two independent sources told me
that the security was full of holes.

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:53.960
Even if the goal was to get the assassins to drop their guard,

00:19:54.700 --> 00:19:57.870
it'd be pointless if you failed to protect those under your care.

00:19:57.870 --> 00:20:01.340
The Ministry of Arms created that lax security regime.

00:20:02.110 --> 00:20:04.450
To be more precise, the Vice Minister.

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:08.860
In other words, he offered to guard the princess,

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:14.750
made the security lax to facilitate the assassins' work, and let them in.

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:17.570
N-No! I didn't do anything like that!

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:19.820
But why would he?

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:23.410
The Vice Minister has a daughter of marriageable age.

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:24.610
Isn't that right?

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:31.490
You wanted your daughter to enter the Imperial Residence.

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:34.850
If the Emperor hadn't said that he'd take only one wife,

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:37.960
you wouldn't have needed to assassinate Jyuusan-hime.

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:42.090
Jyuusan-hime told me that the attacks began after she entered Shishuu,

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:44.310
where she was no longer under the Ran family's protection.

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:49.100
You wanted to assassinate her before she reached Kiyou, but you failed.

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:51.090
Why before Kiyou?

00:20:51.090 --> 00:20:55.790
If Jyuusan-hime were attacked in Kiyou, then it would be normal to assume

00:20:55.790 --> 00:21:00.670
that the culprit was a noble or official who didn't want her to enter the Imperial Residence.

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:03.140
In that case, the Section of Government Inspection would've taken action.

00:21:03.140 --> 00:21:04.380
The Section of Government Inspection?

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:06.700
You'd be in deep trouble if the Section suspected you,

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:08.310
so in order to divert the Section's attention,

00:21:08.310 --> 00:21:10.950
you ordered a phony attack on yourself.

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:12.860
What? Then what happened just now...

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:15.750
You'd say you were attacked and nearly killed,

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:21.670
because you were in charge of guarding Jyuusan-hime and were getting in the assassins' way.

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:25.760
Of course, you made sure the assassins failed to kill you.

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:33.230
But that alone wouldn't be a sufficient mission for Seiga.

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:35.360
Oh? What else, then?

00:21:35.360 --> 00:21:39.030
For example, what if the assassins had orders to kill others?

00:21:39.890 --> 00:21:45.810
Recently, higher officials in the provinces have been dying of suspicious causes.

00:21:45.810 --> 00:21:48.460
All the officials were unrelated.

00:21:48.460 --> 00:21:52.460
However, when you check on the new officials who took over their positions,

00:21:52.460 --> 00:21:54.360
they all have one factor in common.

00:21:54.990 --> 00:21:59.100
They're all related to the Vice Minister of Arms.

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:06.440
Then, don't tell me this man's been using assassins to kill officials?!

00:22:06.690 --> 00:22:10.680
N-No! I-I wouldn't do that.

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:14.030
But you're obviously suspicious.

00:22:14.030 --> 00:22:17.490
Seiga didn't come here to protect the Vice Minister.

00:22:17.490 --> 00:22:21.800
He came to arrest the man who plotted to assassinate Jyuusan-hime and who murdered those officials.

00:22:21.800 --> 00:22:24.300
He protected this man just in case.

00:22:26.720 --> 00:22:28.320
That's right.

00:22:29.440 --> 00:22:31.940
What? He's being too agreeable.

00:22:32.450 --> 00:22:33.720
Something's not right.

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:38.560
Come to think of it, the damage is too great for a sham attack.

00:22:42.190 --> 00:22:45.030
Have I... missed something?

00:22:45.030 --> 00:22:46.980
Jyuusan-hime...

00:22:48.090 --> 00:22:52.720
I was told it was okay to kill Jyuusan-hime and the woman over there!

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:56.970
If I did, I was told they'd keep quiet about the officials!

00:22:56.970 --> 00:22:58.090
But...

00:23:11.050 --> 00:23:12.570
A blow dart.

00:23:12.570 --> 00:23:16.530
One of the assassins must've done it before I got here.

00:24:45.630 --> 00:24:50.050
The assassins were after not only Jyuusan-hime, but me as well?!

00:24:50.050 --> 00:24:52.090
What does this mean?

00:24:52.090 --> 00:24:53.000
Shun-san?

00:24:53.000 --> 00:24:54.790
What? Shusui?!

00:24:54.790 --> 00:24:56.280
What on earth is going on?!
